# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Generated SVG artwork is compared BYTE FOR BYTE against a fresh render by
# test/placeholders.test.mjs. That check is the point: it is what makes a
# generated file reviewable, because a hand-edited SVG then fails the build
# instead of quietly shipping.
#
# It only works if the bytes on disk are the bytes the renderer produced. Under
# `* text=auto` with core.autocrlf=true, checkout rewrites these files to CRLF
# and the comparison fails on files nobody touched - which happened on 2026-10-06
# on a clean tree, where git itself reported no modification.
#
# `-text` marks these as binary for normalisation purposes: no CRLF conversion on
# checkout, no LF conversion on commit. The renderer emits LF, so the bytes now
# survive a round trip unchanged, which is the only way "these bytes are
# reproducible" can mean anything.
*.svg -text

# Same argument, different reason: npm rewrites this file wholesale and it is
# not ours to normalise.
package-lock.json -text
